raining.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Domain Corpus': {'type': ['dataset', 'dataset'], 'description': ['The financial corpus used for further pre-training FinBERT. This is a key step in adapting the model to financial NLP tasks.', 'The financial corpus used for further pre-training FinBERT. This is a key step in adapting the model to financial NLP tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 6]}, 'TRC 2 - financial corpus': {'type': ['DATASET'], 'description': ['A financial corpus used for pre-training the AWD-LSTM language model in ULMFit.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'LSTM classifier': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) based classifier used with GLoVe and ELMo embeddings for contrastive experiments.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'GLoVe embeddings': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Global Vectors for Word Representation, used in the LSTM classifier as a baseline.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'AWD-LSTM language model': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A type of LSTM model used in ULMFit, pre-trained on a financial corpus.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Label imbalance': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The issue of having an uneven distribution of labels in the Financial PhraseBank dataset, with a high percentage of neutral sentences.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Sentence Classification': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The task of categorizing short sentences based on their sentiment, a core objective of the FinBERT model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Accuracy': {'type': ['generic', 'generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the performance of the models.', 'A metric used to measure the performance of the models, specifically how well they differentiate between labels.', 'A performance metric used to evaluate the techniques, specifically mentioned as 0.96 for Vanilla BERT on a subset of Financial Phrasebank.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8, 9, 10]}, 'F1-score': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A metric used to evaluate the performance of the models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'LPS': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'HSC': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'FinSSLX': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model used for comparison in the Financial PhraseBank dataset classification task.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Dropout Probability': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The probability (p = 0.1) used for dropout regularization in the BERT implementation, which helps prevent overfitting.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Warm-up Proportion': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The proportion (0.2) of training steps used for the warm-up phase in the BERT implementation, where the learning rate gradually increases.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Maximum Sequence Length': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ["The maximum number of tokens (64) considered in a sequence during the BERT implementation, influencing the model's input size."], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Learning Rate': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ["The learning rate (2e-05) used to update the model's weights during the BERT implementation, controlling the step size of optimization."], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Mini-batch Size': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The number of samples (64) processed in each mini-batch during the BERT implementation, affecting the training speed and memory usage.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Training Dataset Size': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['The size of the labeled training datasets used to evaluate the performance of the models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'Vanilla BERT': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A version of BERT without further pre-training, used as a baseline for comparison.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'FinBERT - task': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['FinBERT further pre-trained on the classification training set.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'FinBERT - domain': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['FinBERT further pre-trained on a financial domain corpus (TRC 2).'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'TRC 2 - financial': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A financial domain corpus used for further pre-training FinBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [9]}, 'Transformer Encoder Layers': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The architectural component within BERT, with 12 layers in the implemented model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'No adjustment (NA)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ["A setting used to measure the performance of techniques against catastrophic forgetting, where no adjustments are made to the model's training process."], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'Slanted triangular learning rate and gradual unfreezing (STL+GU)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A setting used to measure the performance of techniques against catastrophic forgetting, which combines slanted triangular learning rates with gradual unfreezing.'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'Named Entity Recognition': {'type': ['TASK', 'task'], 'description': ['A subtask of NLP that seeks to locate and classify named entities mentioned in unstructured text into pre-defined categories such as person names, organizations, locations, medical codes, time expressions, quantities, monetary values, percentage, etc.', 'A natural language processing task that involves identifying and classifying named entities (e.g., people, organizations, locations) within text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [11, 11]}, 'Reuters TRC-2 corpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset from Reuters used in the financial domain.'], 'source_chunk_index': [11]}, 'Classification task': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The task that ULMFit was used for, which involved categorizing financial text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [11]}, 'Sentiment Analysis': {'description': ["The process of computationally identifying and categorizing opinions expressed in a piece of text, especially to determine a writer's attitude with respect to a particular topic or document.", 'The process of computationally identifying and categorizing opinions expressed in a piece of text, particularly in the financial domain.', 'The primary task addressed by FinBERT, involving the prediction of sentiment in financial text.', 'The primary NLP task addressed by FinBERT, focusing on determining the sentiment expressed in financial text.', 'The process of determining the emotional tone or attitude expressed within a text, a key application for FinBERT in the financial domain.', 'The process of computationally identifying and categorizing opinions expressed in a piece of text, particularly in the context of financial news articles.', 'The process of determining the emotional tone or attitude expressed in a piece of text, specifically applied to financial news.'], 'type': ['TASK'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 7, 9, 10, 11]}, 'Financial PhraseBank': {'description': ['A dataset used for financial sentiment analysis, created by Malo et al. (2014).', 'A dataset used for evaluating sentiment analysis models in the financial domain.', 'A dataset used for sentiment analysis in financial news, utilized in the study.', 'A dataset used for financial sentiment analysis, utilized in the research for training and evaluating FinBERT.', 'A dataset used for evaluating the performance of FinBERT.'], 'type': ['DATASET'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 10, 11]}, 'Financial Domain': {'description': ['The area of study and application related to finance, including financial markets, institutions, and instruments.', 'The area of finance, including financial news and data.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 3]}, 'NLP (Natural Language Processing)': {'description': ['The field of computer science concerned with giving computers the ability to understand text and spoken words in a human-like manner.', 'A field of computer science and artificial intelligence concerned with the interactions between computers and human (natural) languages, in this context applied to financial text analysis.'], 'type': ['GENERIC', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 11]}, 'Transfer Learning': {'description': ['A machine learning method where a model developed for a task is reused as the starting point for a model on a second task.', 'The method used to leverage pre-trained models like ELMo and ULMFit, and also used in FinBERT.', 'The method used to leverage pre-trained models like BERT to improve performance on financial NLP tasks.', 'The process of using a model trained on one task as the starting point for another task.', 'A machine learning technique used by ULMFit to improve performance on downstream NLP tasks.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2, 4, 7, 9]}, 'Discriminative Fine-tuning': {'description': ["A technique used to optimize FinBERT's performance, likely involving adjusting learning rates for different layers of the model.", "A fine-tuning technique used to optimize FinBERT's performance.", 'Applying different learning rates to different layers of a neural network during fine-tuning.', 'A technique used in ULMFit to fine-tune a pre-trained language model for downstream tasks.', 'A training strategy used during fine-tuning to prevent catastrophic forgetting.', 'A setting used to measure the performance of techniques against catastrophic forgetting, which uses discriminative fine-tuning.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 10, 2, 6]}, 'Slanted Triangular Learning Rates': {'description': ['A learning rate schedule used to optimize FinBERT, potentially involving a gradual increase and decrease of the learning rate during training.', 'A learning rate schedule that increases linearly for a certain number of steps and then decreases linearly.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 10]}, 'Gradual Unfreezing': {'description': ['A technique used to optimize FinBERT, where layers of the model are unfrozen and trained sequentially, starting from the top layers.', 'A technique where layers of a pre-trained model are unfrozen sequentially during fine-tuning.', "A technique used to optimize FinBERT's performance and mitigate catastrophic forgetting."], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 10]}, 'Financial NLP tasks': {'description': ['The specific natural language processing objectives that FinBERT is designed to address within the financial domain, such as sentiment analysis.', 'The field of Natural Language Processing focused on financial text analysis.'], 'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 9]}, 'Pre-trained language models': {'description': ['Models trained on large text corpora and then fine-tuned for specific tasks, such as sentiment analysis.', "A language model that has been trained on a large corpus of text data and can be fine-tuned for various downstream NLP tasks. This is a general concept that is central to the paper's focus on transfer learning."], 'type': ['method', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}, 'Text classification': {'description': ['The task of categorizing text into predefined classes, such as sentiment analysis.', 'The process of categorizing text into predefined classes, relevant in NLP.', 'The task of categorizing text into predefined classes, specifically applied to the financial domain in this context.', 'The task of categorizing text into predefined classes, a core application area for FinBERT.', 'The application of classification techniques to textual data.'], 'type': ['task', 'TASK', 'Task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 6]}, 'GloVe': {'description': ['Global Vectors for Word Representation, a model for generating word embeddings.', 'Global Vectors for Word Representation, a pre-training algorithm.', 'Global Vectors for Word Representation, providing pre-trained word embeddings.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4]}, 'Slanted triangular learning rates': {'description': ['A learning rate schedule used in ULMFit to improve model training.', 'A training strategy used during fine-tuning to prevent catastrophic forgetting.', 'A learning rate schedule that increases linearly for a certain number of steps and then decreases linearly.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 10, 6]}, 'Gradual unfreezing': {'description': ['A technique used in ULMFit to fine-tune a pre-trained language model for downstream tasks.', 'A training strategy used during fine-tuning to prevent catastrophic forgetting.', "A technique used to optimize FinBERT's performance and mitigate catastrophic forgetting."], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 10, 6]}, 'Natural language processing (NLP)': {'description': ['A field of computer science and artificial intelligence concerned with giving computers the ability to understand text and spoken words in much the same way human beings can.', 'A field of computer science and artificial intelligence concerned with the interactions between computers and human (natural) languages, in this context applied to financial text analysis.'], 'type': ['GENERIC', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [11, 3]}, 'Financial PhraseBank dataset': {'description': ['A dataset used for fine-tuning and evaluating the performance of the models, including FinBERT and ULMFit.', 'A dataset used for financial sentiment analysis.', 'The task of classifying sentences from the Financial PhraseBank dataset.'], 'type': ['DATASET', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [8, 7]}, 'Slanted Triangular Learning Rate (STL)': {'description': ["A learning rate strategy used to optimize FinBERT's performance.", 'A learning rate schedule that increases linearly for a certain number of steps and then decreases linearly.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}, 'Slanted triangular learning rate (STL)': {'description': ['A setting used to measure the performance of techniques against catastrophic forgetting, which employs a slanted triangular learning rate.', 'A learning rate schedule that increases linearly for a certain number of steps and then decreases linearly.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [10]}}
